## Mistakes I Made

**Mistake 1 — Misreading the flag**
When I first decrypted the flag I read `CTF{y0u_s0und_th3_backd00r}` instead of `CTF{y0u_f0und_th3_backd00r}`. The letter `f` looked like `s` on screen. 

Lesson: In CTFs, flags are exact. One wrong character = wrong answer. Always read character by character, especially around similar looking characters: `0` vs `O`, `1` vs `l`, `f` vs `s`, `2` vs `z`.

**Mistake 2 — Wrong find command path**
When first running `find` I used a relative path instead of the full absolute path `/tmp/spy_case`. This returned different results.

Lesson: Always use absolute paths (starting with `/`) in commands to avoid path confusion. Absolute paths work from anywhere regardless of your current directory.

